> Results

```
=== Laplacian smoothing ===
Dirichlet energy by iteration (lambda = 0.5):
  iter 0: 404.35
  iter  5: 77.6081
  iter 10: 73.2431
  iter 20: 68.5453
  iter 40: 62.1098

wrote laplacian_smoothing.svg
```

The Dirichlet energy falls monotonically pass after pass \-\- exactly the behavior the test suite checks
across many random meshes \-\- as the interior vertices migrate toward their neighbor averages while the
pinned endpoints anchor the curve.


The red input rattles around the underlying trend; the blue curve, after forty gentle passes, has shed
the jitter and settled onto a smooth arc through the same fixed endpoints. That is discrete heat
diffusion at work: each vertex repeatedly averaged with its neighbors is the explicit Euler step of the
heat equation, and the pinned boundary makes the limit the harmonic (minimal-energy) interpolant.
